      "id": "e3v7mjm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 State at a Glance — Basic Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Karnataka is broadly divided into three main physical divisions: Coastal Plains, Malnad, and Maidan.",
        "The state features major east-flowing rivers like Krishna and Cauvery, alongside west-flowing rivers like Sharavathi and Kali.",
        "Mullayanagiri in the Western Ghats is the highest elevation peak in Karnataka.",
        "The climate is predominantly tropical monsoon with distinct seasonal shifts in rainfall across regions."
      ],
      "id": "mwmdbrs"
    },
